__NAME__ - copy files to standard output

__NAME__ writes each file operand, or standard input, to standard output.


Requirements
------------
A POSIX sh and make.


Installation
------------
__NAME__ is installed into the /usr/local namespace by default; override
PREFIX on the make command line.

Enter the following command to install __NAME__ (if necessary as root):

    make clean install


Running
-------
    __NAME__ [-v] [file...]

See __NAME__(1).


Configuration
-------------
The configuration of __NAME__ is the block of variables at the top of the
script; customisations are kept as patches against it.
